  "findings": [
    "Identical saturated binary-request reservoir pressure maps the fast331-334 burst and nearby slow calls to the sameg although worker call completion patterns differ.",
    "At worst request11 underprediction, both actors have repeated overlapping complete host calls; their real call lengths differ substantially from fixed isolated-profile proxies.",
    "GPU call span includes submission/runtime/driver/device/waiting and cannot establish actual GPU occupancy, active kernels, queue depth, or fair service.",
    "Completion count and rate measured inside the realized foreground wall window are endogenous diagnostic outcomes, not independent causal inputs.",
    "These examples motivate measuring phase-resolved device activity and modeling closed-loop actor/foreground interaction; they do not identify a new service law from heldout data."
  ],
  "future_test": "Use new predeclared pulses/actors and independent device/API/CPU-stage evidence to separate whether long worker host intervals correspond to blocked host, stalled device work, or scheduling/driver interference. Freeze any revised mechanism on new profile data before fresh heldout validation.",
